{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["And I say: We have seen that when Nehemiah went up to Jerusalem, it was in disgrace, as one doomed to die. And now he asks wages and shepherds them with the second staff, and these thirty silver — perhaps they were thirty righteous men who came with him, or in the days of Nehemiah thirty priests served, both great ones and anointed for battle and deputies; therefore it is written השליכהו הכסף אל יוצר (cast the silver to the potter), and it is written כי שם בית ה׳ הוא אדר היקר (for there the house of YHWH is the precious ADAR). יקר is an epithet, like חכם נבון יקר (a wise man of understanding, precious); it is a noun, like ששון (joy) and יקר (preciousness)." "And the word אל (to) serves for another meaning: אל אדר היקר (to the precious ADAR)." "And the meaning of אשר יקרתי (which I prized): the precious house, where My glory dwelt at first — and this is אשר יקרתי מעליהם (which I prized above them), that the glory departed from them in the Second Temple."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "The Hebrew appears to conflate two scriptural citations (Zechariah 11:13 and Ezra 2:59/Nehemiah 7:61); translated hyper-literally as presented."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:51.437268466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}